key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T16:10:00-07:00","id":1487948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aether/1486260-tc-aether-kickstarter?p=1487822#post1487822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I presume the third one is Philip Wylie's 1930 novel Gladiator. The other two I'm not familiar with. </div> </div> </div> </div>You got number three. The first one is from an Italian author who is obscure in Italy. His name is Tarchetti. The middle one is a German story, and it was adapted for something like the X-Files <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While a thread with interesting ideas - especially period ones - for Magogs might be useful and interesting, right now I'm just lamenting that the Magag preview from this weekend's kickstarter update didn't have such examples while the Squire and Gog ones did. (Because vision issues make it extremely difficult for me to read most PDF files unless I physically print them out, I've no idea if such examples are already in the final draft or not.) </div> </div> </div>Good point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-25-2022, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T19:12:39-07:00","id":1487963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aether/1486260-tc-aether-kickstarter?p=1487948#post1487948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first one is from an Italian author who is obscure in Italy. His name is Tarchetti.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iginio Ugo Tarchetti. The story in question appears to be his fairly blatant plagiarization of Mary Shelly's &quot;The Mortal Immortal&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the KS seems to be powering through the stretch goals. I'm looking forward to more period characters. <br /> <br /> Beyond the core book, it occurs to me that a sourcebook about going to the Moon, Mars, and Venus, either as explorers or to take the fight to the Martians, would be pretty awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 07-25-2022, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-conseq